# Test: an operational command argument outside its YANG enumeration is
# refused with the same refusal as a config value, on the daemon route.
# QUESTION: does an operator who types `send bgp <peer> raw gzip <hex>` read the
# argument, the value, every accepted encoding with its help, and the whole
# command to type with the placeholder in place of gzip? A unit test builds the
# definitions by hand; only the shipped YANG and the real dispatcher reached
# through `ze cli -c` prove the help is read from the model and the route
# restates the one fault.
# VALIDATES: AC-12 (spec-config-enum-refusal-proposes-valid-values).
# PREVENTS: `invalid value "gzip", expected one of: hex, b64`.
#
# Method: the daemon runs one SSH server on 127.0.0.1 $PORT, which the CLI dials.
# No BGP peer is configured: the refusal is the dispatcher's, before the handler.

option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ZE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.
option=env:var=XDG_DATA_HOME:value=.
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass

stdin=init-answers:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
testpass
127.0.0.1
$PORT
EOF_INIT

tmpfs=refusal.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze init:stdin=init-answers:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze start refusal.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.

# One value fault: the whole command is the fix, the placeholder in place.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze cli -c "send bgp 192.0.2.1 raw gzip DEADBEEF"
expect=stderr:contains=raw encoding: "gzip" is not an accepted value
expect=stderr:contains=encoding accepts only these values:
expect=stderr:contains=fix: send bgp 192.0.2.1 raw <hex|b64> DEADBEEF
reject=stderr:contains=expected one of
reject=stderr:contains=faults, so Ze did not run it

# A close value is named and put in the fix.
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze cli -c "send bgp 192.0.2.1 raw hx DEADBEEF"
expect=stderr:contains="hx" is not an accepted value (did you mean hex?)
expect=stderr:contains=fix: send bgp 192.0.2.1 raw hex DEADBEEF
